WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 line:92%
-Congratulations on the film.

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations on
your Golden Globe nomination.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks so much.
-For those who haven't seen,

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:07.207
this is one of the great stunt
driving films of the modern era.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.210
And is it true that you did
some of the stunt driving?

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I did all --
No, I did some of it.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.246 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
They didn't let me do
that much stunt driving.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:17.617
-So what would they let you do,
like, parallel park?

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.151 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.687
-No, they did not -- definitely
did not let me parallel park.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.588 line:92%
No. Just regular parking.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:24.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
The problem -- So, I did
like 10 stunt driving classes.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I actually learned how to
drive most of the stuff.

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is before the movie
started, you put the work in.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:34.834
-I put the work in. I wanted to
know how to drive like Baby.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:35.268 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:38.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But then when I actually
got on set,

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Okay, what are we doing?

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What are we doing?"

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said,
"You're not doing anything."

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We got Jamie Foxx in the car
and Jon Hamm in the car.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're not doing anything."
-Right.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:47.280 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-You know what I mean?

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.716
And then when Jamie Foxx
and Jon Hamm weren't in the car,

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:50.550 line:92%
then they let me do stuff.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, interesting.
-Yeah.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:54.254 size:84% position:42%
-So they didn't want to
risk the whole cast?

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, just me.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just part of it, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:59.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, well,
it certainly paid off.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
You actually kept the car.
Is this true?

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.530
'Cause I don't think --
I've never heard of this.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like in
the "Fast and Furious" movies,

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:06.699 line:92%
they don't get to keep the car.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.302
-Really? You don't think
Vin Diesel has a garage of like,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
a hundred of the
"Fast and Furious" cars?

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.206
-Of course he does.
I don't know what I'm thinking.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Totally does.
-Of course he does.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, no, I saw Vin Diesel
on the bus.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. I don't think --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you got to keep your car.
-Yes.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.582 size:88% position:44%
-What kind of car is it?
-It's a Subaru WRX STI.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the one
from the opening scene.

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:25.485 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Gotcha.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:27.253
-And I just kept begging
for them to let me have it.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then I said, "I'll buy it.
I'll do whatever."

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just kept following up
and e-mailing.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's how --
if you want something in life,

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
you just keep following up.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:36.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Go get 'em.
-Yeah.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
I kept e-mailing the producers
and saying,

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.166 line:92%
"Hey, how about that car?

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:42.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
I'm willing to pay for it.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:42.836 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Let me get that car."

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:45.538 size:88% position:44%
And then months later,
when it was my birthday,

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
about six months later,
they gave it to me.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You wore them down.
Congratulations.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-That's really nice.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:55.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Perseverance.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, so that --
For fans of the film,

00:01:57.484 --> 00:02:00.353
it must be an interesting thing
to see you

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.155 line:92%
in the car from the movie.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:02.555 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.758
-I mean, you know, you don't see
Christian Bale in the Batmobile.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:09.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, my other question is
do people also --

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has anybody picked up
on calling you Baby yet?

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because that is
obviously a unique name

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.301 line:92%
for a main character in a film.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:19.506
-Yeah, it's a little odd because
people do call me Baby now.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:22.842
There's this deli around the
corner of my house in Brooklyn.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:25.345
And the guys are nice
and they were always nice to me

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.981 size:84% position:42%
for the first two years
that I've lived there

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:28.815 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and gone in there.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:29.482 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But now, I walk in there

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:32.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this dude from Yemen is
like, "Hey, baby!"

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:32.685 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.288
"What do you want? You want
the halal over rice, man?"

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:35.722 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:38.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, Baby, come on. Make
a halal over rice for Baby."

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:38.658 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nothing would make me happier
than if you found out

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's never seen the film.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:45.598 size:88% position:44%
He just -- That after --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
Basically, like, hey,
you know...

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.504
Anyone -- it turns out anyone
that goes there for two years,

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.640
he just feels comfortable enough
with them

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
to finally start
calling them Baby.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:56.409 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Could be.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Jamie Foxx,
one of your cast members --

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
cast mates of the show --
uh, film.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:02.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
He would deejay on set.
This film is so tied to music.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he would actually deejay
in between takes.

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:07.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that when he would do it?
-Yeah.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.189 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So, Jamie does deejay.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:12.492
And he wouldn't have turntables
on set.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:15.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he would connect
his boom box to his phone

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
and start playing music
between takes.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:18.464 line:92%
And the whole crew loved it,

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.700 size:75% position:38%
especially on, like,
late night shoots.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.401 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It would be 4:00 A.M.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people are tired
and it keeps the energy up.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.938 size:78% position:39%
-And he's good at it?
He's a good deejay.

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:28.041
-He's great. And he also -- you
know, he sort of ad-libs too.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:30.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He does like
the, "Yeah, come on!"

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:30.777 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right.
He's his own hype man.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he hypes up
the whole crew.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:34.881 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was really fun.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:35.915 size:88% position:44% line:92%
So, then I figure, like,

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was a great thing to do
on a set.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the next movie
I did after "Baby Driver"

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
was this movie
called "Jonathan."

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the first day
we were in a bar,

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:48.761
so I actually found, like,
these turntables and a cord

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:49.429 size:75% position:38% line:92%
to plug my phone in.

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I figured it would have
a great sound system.

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:54.567
And I thought, "What would be a
fun song to play for the crew?"

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.568 line:92%
And this is a morning shoot,

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it's a little early,
about 6:00 A.M.,

00:03:57.103 --> 00:04:00.073
and I decided to play Haddaway,
"What is Love?" You know?

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ What is love ♪♪
-Yeah sure.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.142 size:78% position:39%
♪♪ -Baby, don't -- ♪♪
So I plugged that in,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I didn't quite turn
the sound down right away.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:08.081 line:92%
And it blasted ♪♪ What is love ♪♪

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:10.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the whole crew
starts looking, like,

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:10.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"What's going on?"

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.518
The first A.D. is like,
"Where's that music coming from?

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.320
Where's that music coming from?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Oh, it's me. It's me."

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like,
"Can you turn that off?"

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:17.957 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"I'm not Jamie Foxx."

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:23.329
-I think, yeah, in general,
for people like you and I,

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:26.065
don't ever try to do the things
Jamie Foxx is good at.

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:26.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. I mean, I try.
-Yeah.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.502
-I will continue to try to do
everything Jamie Foxx does.

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, you gave six months
and you got that car.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:32.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
Keep at this, too.
-Yeah.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:35.174 size:75% position:38%
-I'm doing to deejay
on every set I'm on.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.809 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Eventually it will work.

